00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.500
into the back of his own hand. She tries to fight back via repeated regenerations

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:38.260
but eventually succumbs to the flames. What a casual viewer might see is one of the most exciting and badass

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:43.240
moments of the show, is a moment I see as the key to this entire theory.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:46.760
As I established in my last episode about Full Metal Alchemist, human bodies in this

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:50.800
fictional universe are made of the same stuff as human bodies in our universe.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:55.120
They give us the explicit formula in the show and it matches real life - one for one.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.599
So if we can figure out how much energy is contained within a human body, we can extrapolate from there

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.940
how much energy it would take Lust to regenerate that body after Mustang

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:08.240
serves it up extra-crispy style. AND, based on how many times she gets burned before being completely

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:12.960
roasted, we can figure out exactly how much energy is contained within her Philosopher's Stone.

00:05:13.169 --> 00:05:16.960
Then from there, divide it by the number of souls in the stone and voila,

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:21.080
we have calculated the amount of energy one human soul contains.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.120
Isn't math great?

